From b15bf89460a7f7fe464be9a7d24786788ffc2f38 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 14:32:10 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 047/122] TABLESTYLE: read all R2010+ cell styles, R2007 row
 style values

- R2010+: the cell styles after the table cell style are an array
  (ovr, numoverrides; _TITLE, _HEADER, _DATA with ids 1, 2, 3), each
  after a BL (index, 1-3), as ACadSharp readTableStyle. Only the first was
  read: example_2018 0x29B ended at 310.4 with 6688 unknown bits, now at
  734.4 = bitsize - 17 - data_size, the text style handles point to the
  STYLE Standard (0x11). Same for sample_AC1024..AC1032.
- R2007: the row styles have the value data type, unit type and format
  string after the borders (20.4.101.1); rows 1 and 2 of example_2007 and
  sample_AC1021 were garbage, now the data ends at the string stream.
  rowstyles[].format_string is T, not TU.
- downconvert_TABLESTYLE rewritten: the data, title and header row
  styles from _DATA, _TITLE and _HEADER (else the table cell style), the
  margins and the flow direction from the table cell style, a "none"
  background as ACI 7 without background, the border invisibility (BL 93)
  inverted, missing borders visible ByBlock. New allocations without
  color names and global handles, freed by free_TABLESTYLE_r2010, which
  also frees the cell styles (the spec does not when writing R2000). The
  encoder converts before the margins, not after (they were 0).
- in_dxf TABLESTYLE: colors as table colors (ACI 7 is 0xc3000007, not the
  palette RGB), border lineweights as given (-2 ByBlock, not the entity
  lineweight index), 420-427 as 24-bit RGB.
- JSON: ovr is an array (numoverrides); dynapi, dynapi_test, dynapi.texi.

Checked: the DXF TABLESTYLE of example_2000..2018.dwg equals AutoCAD's
example_2000..2018.dxf (except handles; example_2010/2013.dxf have an
xdictionary the DWG has not). The TABLESTYLE of the R2000 output of
dwgrewrite and of dwg2dxf -> dxf2dwg equals AutoCAD's R2000
example_2000.dwg (and example_2004.dwg) for example_2007..2018, and
AutoCAD's sample_AC1015.dwg for sample_AC1021..AC1032. ACadSharp's
DxfReader reads the DXF without TextStyle/TableStyle warnings. JSON of
example_2018 written to R2000 gives the same table style.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
